## Findings

### 1. HIGH (tests): bind-session tests read the real home, take 92 % of the suite, are flaky without it, and leak folders with real transcript metadata (7 October 2026)
- Code path: `AssetsService` constructor `scripts/AssetsService.mjs:217` builds `createConversationCatalog({ stateDir, fileToken })` without `home`, so `ConversationCatalog.mjs:27` defaults to `process.env.HOME` and walks `~/.claude/projects`, `~/.codex/sessions`, Gemini and Claude Desktop folders. `bind-session` (`AssetsService.mjs:1220`) calls `conversationIndexSync.request(id, { immediate: true })`, which runs `catalog.list()` plus `linkConversations` over every real transcript (`ConversationIndexSync.mjs:91-92`). The test fixture (`AssetsService.test.js:398-413`) cannot inject a home because the constructor has no option for it. (7 October 2026)
- Second defect: `afterEach` runs cleanup FIFO (`AssetsService.test.js:397`), and the fixture pushes `rm(root)` (line 400) BEFORE `service.close()` (line 411). The temp root is deleted while the index sync still writes, and `writeJsonAtomic` (`ConversationLinks.mjs:126-129`) recreates it with `mkdir -p`. (7 October 2026)
- MEASURED: same 4 tests, real HOME: 21.89 s, 4 pass. With `HOME=<empty dir>`: 0.96 s, but 3 then 2 of 4 FAIL (`ENOTEMPTY ... /state`), so the green result depends on the scan being slow enough. Commands: `./node_modules/.bin/vitest run scripts/AssetsService.test.js -t "session bindings|idempotently|actual conversation agent"` with and without `HOME=.../scratch-maint/emptyhome`. (7 October 2026)
- MEASURED leak: `ls -d $TMPDIR/zr-assets-test-* | wc -l` = 35 folders, 3.6 MB, four per suite run since 10:28 today (commit d910105e added the immediate index sync). Each holds `state/ConversationLinks.json` (129,816 bytes, 484 entries of real transcript paths). Isolated cost of one cold catalog+link pass on this Mac: `catalog.list()` 474 ms, full `flush()` 1,930 ms (node -e scripts in scratch-maint). (7 October 2026)
- Fix (S): add constructor options `conversationHome` (default `process.env.HOME`) and optionally `conversationCatalog`, pass `home: path.join(root, 'home')` in the fixture; make cleanup LIFO (`cleanup.unshift(...)` or iterate reversed) so `service.close()` awaits the running sync before `rm`; add one assertion that no `ConversationLinks.json` mentions a path outside the temp root. Expected suite time about 3 s. (7 October 2026)

### 2. HIGH (maintainability, perf side effect): `inventory()` is a god method that also republishes the global index of all 18 projects (7 October 2026)
- Code path: `inventory()` `AssetsService.mjs:294-354` = scan + version comparison + `save()` (32 MB JSON) + `refreshContextIndex()` (lines 357-375: `snapshot()` of EVERY project, `GlobalProjectIndex.json`, 18 markdown files) + `scheduleSceneAudits()`. It has 21 call sites (`grep -n "await this.inventory(" scripts/AssetsService.mjs`); an archive with version preservation runs it at 631, 612 (per conflict), 627, 687; restore runs 696 then 810 or 727; every `checkpoint` (1304) and every scene audit timer (1018). (7 October 2026)
- MEASURED on a copy of the real state (18 projects, 72 MB) with `new AssetsService(config, { getToken: throw, runProcess: throw }).initialize()` pointed at `scratch-maint/statecopy`: `snapshot()` of all projects 983 ms (mostly synchronous), vegetation alone 223 ms, `refreshContextIndex()` 926 ms and 914 ms, `save(vegetation)` 48 ms, cloud snapshot vegetation 282 ms. So each inventory of a 3-file project still pays about 0.9 s of whole-system work, and the `list` action the UI polls (`AssetsWorkspaceView.jsx:141`, `AssetsService.mjs:1321-1325`) pays the 983 ms again. (7 October 2026)
- Fix (M): split into `scanProject(id)` (pure: returns inventory, no I/O beyond reading sources) and `commitInventory(id)` (save); replace the inline `refreshContextIndex()` with `contextIndexChanged(id)` that coalesces bursts like `ConversationIndexSync.schedule` (quiet window, max wait) and recomputes only the touched project's mapping; keep an explicit `await refreshContextIndex()` only where a caller returns the index (`global-index`, `bind-session`). (7 October 2026)

### 3. HIGH (tests): the archive and restore engines are never exercised; their output contract only exists in hand-written fakes (7 October 2026)
- Code path: `archiveNow` spawns `scripts/archive-folder.mjs` (1,639 lines) at `AssetsService.mjs:662` and parses `{ev:'done', verifyKo, skipped}` (665) plus an index `{dest, at, fiches:[{rel, sha, taille, manifeste}]}` (666-675); `restoreOriginal` spawns `Cloud/scripts/restaurer.mjs` (827) and expects `{ev:'restaure', cible}` (831). In tests `runProcess` is always a stub (`AssetsService.test.js:410` throws, fakes at 520, 675, 697-698, 740, 855-856); `grep -rl "archive-folder\|restaurer" --include='*.test.*'` finds no test that runs either engine. (7 October 2026)
- Impact ESTIMATED: a rename of one field in the engine (they are French: `fiches`, `taille`, `manifeste`, `restaure`, `cible`) keeps 120 tests green and makes every production backup fail with "Archive engine did not confirm every selected file" or a fingerprint mismatch. This is the path that moves 10.4 GB for vegetation. (7 October 2026)
- Fix (M): one contract test that runs the real `archive-folder.mjs --json --index=...` and `restaurer.mjs` against a local fake drive API (`ZR_API_BASE` is already passed at `AssetsService.mjs:642`) on 3 tiny files, asserting the exact event and index shape; export the event names and index field names from one module (e.g. `scripts/lib/archive-contract.mjs`) imported by the engine, the service and the fakes. (7 October 2026)

### 4. MEDIUM (maintainability): `request()` is a 270-line string dispatcher and the class carries about 11 responsibilities (7 October 2026)
- Evidence: `request()` spans `AssetsService.mjs:1084-1354` with about 30 `if (action === ...)` branches; `start` alone is 1224-1292 and embeds two Markdown templates, a hardcoded absolute doctrine path `/Users/zenray/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (1279), `Europe/Paris` (1278), category default `'Projet'` (1232) and a `python3` spawn (1286); `checkpoint` spawns `python3` again (1303). The class also owns state persistence, event log, inventory, context index, scene audits, scene preparation, archive, restore, extend, unload, recover, watcher, conversations, previews and HTTP. 107,332 bytes, 43 lines over 200 characters. (7 October 2026)
- Impact ESTIMATED: every change touches the file whose SHA-256 is pinned by `scripts/Assets/SkillContract.json`, so unrelated edits collide; internal calls go back through the public dispatcher (`this.request('history')` 576, `this.request('scene-context')` 1023, `this.request('scene-preparation-plan')` 1129/1133, `this.request('bind-session')` 1288), which hides dependencies. (7 October 2026)
- Fix (L, staged): a handler table `{ action: handler }` with per-action payload validation, then modules: `ProjectStateStore`, `InventoryService`, `WorkspaceLifecycle` (archive/restore/extend/unload/recover), `SceneAudits`, `ConversationFacade`, `ProjectInitializer` (templates in `scripts/Assets/templates/`), `HttpBridge`. Internal callers call the module method, not `request()`. (7 October 2026)

### 5. MEDIUM (tests): the HTTP boundary and the production composition root have zero tests, and there are two divergent entry points (7 October 2026)
- Evidence: `handleHttp` (`AssetsService.mjs:1356-1394`: loopback check, origin allow-list, `x-zr-assets-client`, auth, 256 KiB body limit, JSON errors) is never called by a test (`grep -c handleHttp scripts/AssetsService.test.js` = 0). Production runs `Daemon.mjs serve` -> `local-server.mjs`, which wires the cloud publisher, `conversationMirror.start()`, `conversationIndexSync.start()` and `feedbackCapture` (`local-server.mjs:32-39`); `AssetsService.mjs main('serve')` (1451-1461) wires none of them and nothing launches it (`grep -rn AssetsService.mjs` shows only imports). `Daemon.mjs` passes `ZENRAY_API_SECRET: ''`, so the auth branch (1375-1379) never runs in production while `BridgeClient.mjs` still sends the secret. (7 October 2026)
- Fix (S-M): extract `createAssetsRuntime({ port })` from `local-server.mjs` and test it with fakes (publisher, mirror, sync and capture started; close stops them); add handleHttp tests (403 non-loopback, 403 bad origin, 403 missing client header, 413 body, 400 bad JSON, 200 status); delete `main('serve')` or make it call the same runtime. (7 October 2026)

### 6. MEDIUM (maintainability): the same low-level helpers are re-implemented several times (7 October 2026)
- Atomic write, five copies with three temp-naming schemes and two indentations: `atomicJson` (`AssetsService.mjs:38-43`, pid+UUID, indent 2), inline in `refreshContextIndex` (366-369, UUID), `writeJsonAtomic` (`ConversationLinks.mjs:126-129`, pid only, indent 1, and `mkdir -p` that resurrects deleted folders, see finding 1), `ConversationIndexSync.mjs:39-41` (pid only), `ConversationMirror.mjs:52-57`. (7 October 2026)
- `SessionBindings.json`, declared "the unique session/project link", is parsed by 7 independent readers: `AssetsService.mjs:359, 1206, 1298`, `AssetsFeedbackCapture.mjs:68`, `ConversationIndexSync.mjs:69`, `BeginConversation.mjs:16`, `LinkConversations.mjs:16`, `ConversationCatalog.mjs:45`; only `bind-session` takes the lock. (7 October 2026)
- Symlink-safe directory creation duplicated: `prepareWorkspaceDirectory` (738-747) and the inline copy in `start` (1259-1267). Descriptor-verified hashing duplicated: `hashLocalFile(file, token)` (144-159) and `scene-context` (1152-1161). Loaded-workspace commit (baselines + `workspacePath` + restorations + `watcher.suivre`) duplicated in `restoreNow` 719-724, `recoverNow` 926-932 and partly `extendWorkspace` 804-806. Selection validation duplicated 1337-1338 / 1343-1344. `'Current.json'` path rebuilt 5 times. (7 October 2026)
- Fix (M): `scripts/lib/atomic-file.mjs` (one writer, UUID temp, no implicit parent creation for state roots), `scripts/Assets/SessionBindingsStore.mjs` (read, bind under lock, validate), `ensureManagedDirectory`, `hashVerifiedDescriptor`, `commitLoadedWorkspace(id, loaded, attempt)`, `workspacePaths(id)`. Behaviour-identical extractions, guarded by the existing 120 tests. (7 October 2026)

### 7. MEDIUM (maintainability, HDA): values written in two or more places instead of `AssetsConfig.json` (7 October 2026)
- Bridge port 3100 and timeout 30000: `AssetsConfig.json bridge.port/requestTimeoutMs`, `Daemon.mjs:10` (`port: 3100`, plus its own `runtime` folder duplicating `storage.stateDir`), `src/lib/projectBridge.js` `PROJECT_BRIDGE_CONFIG` (`localOrigin: 'http://localhost:3100'`, `timeoutMs: 30000`), `scripts/Assets/CheckPreview.mjs`. (7 October 2026)
- Preview TTL `600000` at `AssetsService.mjs:1193` and `1406`; image extensions as a regex (1192) and again as a MIME map (1410) although text previews already live in `PROJECT_PREVIEW_CONFIG`; loopback list at 1359 and 1399 (and `Freelance/Service.mjs:8`); scene regex `/\.hip(?:lc|nc)?$/i` at 992 and 1148; `rm` retry `maxRetries: 5, retryDelay: 200` three times; `inventoryDebounceMs ?? 1000` (979) repeats the config default; engine script paths at 567, 662, 827; `storage.maxEvents` caps both events (290) and persisted job ids (502). (7 October 2026)
- Agent list `['claude','codex','gemini','antigravity']` at 1199, 1296 and `ConversationIdentity.mjs:5`; session-id regex differs: `/^[a-zA-Z0-9-]{8,128}$/` at 1200, 1229 and `ConversationIdentity.mjs:6`, but `/^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$/` (any length, underscore allowed) for `checkpoint` (1296). A checkpoint can therefore be written for a session id that `bind-session` can never bind, and the binding check at 1298-1299 passes because no binding exists. (7 October 2026)
- Fix (S): add `bridge.localOrigin`, `preview.ttlMs`, `preview.imageTypes` (ext -> MIME), `bridge.loopback`, `agents`, `sessionIdPattern`, `sceneExtensions`, `engines.{archive,restore,index}`, `storage.maxJobs`, `fs.rmRetries`; `Daemon.mjs` and `projectBridge.js` read them (the front end can import the JSON at build time). Defaults equal the current values, so no behaviour changes except the checkpoint pattern, which should use the shared one. (7 October 2026)

### 8. MEDIUM (maintainability, io-state): project state files carry no schema version and their shape is defined in several places (7 October 2026)
- MEASURED: the 18 `Project-*.json` files have 4 different key sets (10, 11, 12 and 14 keys) and 0 carry `schemaVersion` (node loop over the files, 7 October 2026). Defaults are written twice (`{ backups: {}, restorations: {}, watched: false, jobs: [] }` at 251 and 491) and fields appear lazily through 7 `||= {}` (`productionBaselines` x4 at 618/719/804/926, `preservedOriginalVersions` 620, `sceneAudits` 1164, `scenePreparations` 1136). Vegetation: `backups` 16.6 MB (durable proof) and `inventory` 11.9 MB (derived, rebuildable) live in the same 32.5 MB file; `jobs` keeps 80 ids whose objects are lost on restart. (7 October 2026)
- Impact ESTIMATED: any change of a stored field has no migration path and no place to declare it; a rollback after a refactor cannot tell which writer produced a file. (7 October 2026)
- Fix (M): `ProjectStateStore` with `createProjectState()`, `migrateProjectState(raw)` keyed on `schemaVersion` (absent = 1), written on every save; optionally move `inventory` to `Inventory-<id>.json` so a corrupt cache never touches the backup proofs. (7 October 2026)

### 9. MEDIUM (tests, robustness): repeated linear searches inside batch loops (7 October 2026)
- `archiveNow` resolves each snapshotted file with `index.fiches.find((entry) => entry.rel.normalize('NFC') === file.relativePath)` (`AssetsService.mjs:669`) inside the per-batch loop; the index accumulates every file of the source (real `indexes/*/workshop.json` up to 7.7 MB). MEASURED synthetic (node -e, 18,238 fiches, 200 lookups, 7 October 2026): 342 ms per batch versus 6.5 ms with a Map. With 200 files per batch, the 18,238-file vegetation project needs about 92 batches, about 31 s of blocked event loop (ESTIMATED from the synthetic number). (7 October 2026)
- The same pattern `inventory.localFiles.find((entry) => entry.id === ...)` appears 9 times (328, 387, 615, 1002, 1019, 1147, 1173, 1191, 1407), plus `project.sources.find` by id 7 times. (7 October 2026)
- Fix (S): build `new Map(index.fiches.map(...))` once per batch; keep `filesById` / `sourcesById` maps next to the inventory (rebuilt in `commitInventory`). (7 October 2026)

### 10. LOW (robustness, tests): watcher recovery is detected by matching French UI text, through a positional callback contract compiled at runtime (7 October 2026)
- `createWatcher` (`AssetsService.mjs:937-970`) treats a report as a recovery when `/rétablie/.test(detail)` (958), matching the human message `'surveillance du dossier rétablie'` in `Cloud/electron/watcher.ts:60`; the same text is the exported `watch` event. The watcher takes 6 positional callbacks (951-964). It is compiled at startup with `esbuild`, which is not declared in `package.json` (present only through `vite@5.4.21 -> esbuild@0.21.5`, `npm ls esbuild`). Tests inject `watchFactory` 8 times, so neither the compilation nor the real message is exercised. (7 October 2026)
- Fix (S): the watcher reports `{ sourceKey, state: 'recovered' | 'failed', message }`; constructor takes an options object; declare `esbuild` in devDependencies or precompile `watcher.ts`; one test with the real compiled watcher on a temp folder. (7 October 2026)

