## Refactor order that does not break the running service (7 October 2026)

The LaunchAgent runs `Daemon.mjs serve` -> `local-server.mjs` from the working tree; Node loads modules once at start, so edits do not affect the running process until it restarts. Each step: suite green, `node scripts/Assets/CheckSkillContract.mjs` updated (any NEW module must be added to `requiredFiles` in `CheckSkillContract.mjs:17`, otherwise the contract silently stops covering the moved code), skill section appended, commit, push. Restart once per step, only when `list` shows no running job (an interrupted job is resumable, but a restart mid-archive repeats work). (7 October 2026)

1. Tests first, no production change: hermetic home option with unchanged default, LIFO cleanup (finding 1); handleHttp tests and runtime composition test (5); engine contract test (3); a state fixture built from the 4 real key shapes (8). (7 October 2026)
2. Behaviour-identical extractions: atomic writer, SessionBindingsStore, ensureManagedDirectory, hashVerifiedDescriptor, commitLoadedWorkspace, Map lookups (6, 9). (7 October 2026)
3. Config values into `AssetsConfig.json` with defaults equal to today, including Daemon and projectBridge (7); align the checkpoint session pattern. (7 October 2026)
4. `ProjectStateStore` with `schemaVersion` and a migration that reads every old shape; keep reading old files for one release so a rollback stays possible (8). (7 October 2026)
5. Handler table for `request()`, then module split (4); structured watcher status (10); delete dead code (11). (7 October 2026)
6. Last, the only step that changes timing: decouple `inventory()` from `refreshContextIndex()` with a coalesced, per-project index refresh (2); verify after restart that `GlobalProjectIndex.json` and `contexts/*.md` are regenerated within the quiet window and that `context <id>` still answers. (7 October 2026)
